# ArogyaNav — Smart Indoor Hospital Navigation

> 🏥 **Running at:** http://localhost:5173

## Tech Stack
| Tool | Version | Purpose |
|------|---------|---------|
| Vite | 8.x | Build tool & dev server |
| React | 19 | UI framework |
| html5-qrcode | latest | Camera + QR decoding |
| lucide-react | latest | Icon set |
| Vanilla CSS | — | Design system |

---

## Project Structure

```
src/
├── index.css               # Full design system (tokens, components, animations)
├── main.jsx                # App entry point
├── App.jsx                 # Root: step bar + screen routing
├── components/
│   ├── QrScannerView.jsx   # Screen 1 — Camera scanner
│   ├── DestinationView.jsx # Screen 2 — Department search & select
│   └── NavigationView.jsx  # Screen 3 — Step-by-step directions
└── data/
    └── hospitalData.js     # Location map, department list, route generator
```

---

## Screens

### Screen 1 — QR Scanner
- Opens device camera via `html5-qrcode`
- Scans and validates location IDs against `HOSPITAL_LOCATIONS` map
- Graceful fallback if camera is unavailable (demo button always works)
- Animated scan-line overlay with corner brackets

### Screen 2 — Destination Selection
- Shows current scanned location badge
- Live search filter across all 12 departments
- Scrollable department cards with icon, description, floor, and wing
- Accessible: keyboard navigable, ARIA roles

### Screen 3 — Navigation
- Destination header card (gradient blue)
- Meta chips: total distance + estimated walk time + current step
- **Directional arrow card** — large arrow (↑ ↗ ↙) with colour-coded background
- Prev / Next step buttons
- Collapsible "All Steps" list with click-to-jump
- "Scan Again" button to reset the entire flow

